  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "сети",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the plural for nets, and the singular also means a computer network.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Берите большие и маленькие.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Take the big and small ones.' Russian drops 'nets' here, since everybody knows what's meant. The two describing words stand alone.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Берите всё, что у нас есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Take everything that we have.' We will examine the sentence: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "у",
